    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0541, En Con L (as proposed in S.3163 & A.1819)",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8773\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nalternatives for the use of pesticides in the monarch preservation plan\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to L.2025, C.620.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by refining the agency's\nrole regarding alternative pest management practices and clarifying when\nagricultural land is subject to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 620 of the Laws of 2025.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2025 amending the environmental conservation law\nrelating to enacting the monarch preservation plan, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S.3163 and A.1819, takes effect.\n",
